profiles/agw.json says what AppleGamingWiki (https://www.applegamingwiki.com) reports about running
each game on a Mac. It is taken from the "macOS Compatibility" table on each game's page there, by the
AppleGamingWiki contributors, and is licensed, like the wiki, under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported licence:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/

Changes made by Nightforge (scripts/fetch-agw.py): only the table's ratings for the native, Rosetta 2,
CrossOver and Wine ways and their notes are kept; wiki markup and references are removed, notes are
shortened, and the versions, graphics layers, DirectX versions, Apple chips and dates the notes name are
listed per way. "hint" is Nightforge's own reading of these. Each entry names its page; the page is at
https://www.applegamingwiki.com/wiki/<page>.

Steam app IDs for pages without an infobox come from Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), CC0.

